\viewkind4\uc1\pard\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1.\cf0   Deck thyself, my soul, with gladness,
\par \pard\li144\sl190\slmult0  Leave the gloomy haunts of sadness,
\par  Come into the daylight's splendour,
\par   There with joy thy praises render
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par   Unto Him whose grace unbounded
\par  Hath this wondrous banquet founded;
\par  High o'er all the heav'ns He reigneth,
\par  Yet to dwell with thee He deigneth.
\par 
\par \pard\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  2.  Hasten as a bride to meet Him,
\par \pard\li144\sl190\slmult0  And with loving reverence greet Him,
\par  For with words of life immortal
\par  Now He knocketh at thy portal;
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6  Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Haste to ope the gates before Him,
\par  Saying, while thou dost adore Him,
\par  'Suffer, Lord, that I receive Thee,
\par  And I never more will leave Thee.'
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Sun, who all my life dost brighten;\cf0 
\par \pard\li180\sl190\slmult0 Light, who dost my soul enlighten;
\par Joy, the sweetest man e'er knoweth;
\par Fount, whence all my being floweth:
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par At Thy feet I cry, my Maker,
\par Let me be a fit partaker
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0  Of this blessed food from heav'n,
\par \pard\li180\sl190\slmult0 For our good, Thy glory, given.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-180\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Jesus, Bread of Life, I pray Thee,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj Let me gladly here obey Thee;
\par Never to my hurt invited,
\par Be Thy love with love requited:
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj From this banquet let me measure,
\par Lord, how vast and deep its treasure;
\par Through the gifts Thou here dost give me,
\par As Thy guest in heav'n receive me.
\par \pard\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs14 
\par }

